 nonzero finitely generated R-submodule of Q. Clearing denominators gives a nonzero finitely generated ideal dI of R. Each nonzero q in Q has form p^k u with integer k and u a unit of R. For any nonzero finitely generated ideal, take the least exponent k among a finite set of nonzero generators: all generators lie in p^k R and one is p^k times a unit, so the ideal is p^k R. Thus dI is principal and J is free of rank one. Choose a generator a; then a e_i form an R-basis of M_R. On this basis x(ae_i)=(lambda-i+1)ae_(i-1), y(ae_i)=(i+1)ae_(i+1), and h(ae_i)=(lambda-2i)ae_i, with out-of-range terms zero. Reduction modulo p therefore gives the standard module. Also M_R/pM_R is M tensor_Z F_p: a Z-basis of M gives the same reduced basis and reduced integral action matrices. Extending scalars from F_p to K gives an L(K)-module isomorphism with the standard module over K. For r<=lambda<p, r! is invertible modulo p, so X_r and Y_r are scalar multiples of powers of x and y. The matrix-unit identities remain valid modulo p since binom(lambda,j) is nonzero there. Any K-subspace W invariant under x,y,h is invariant under every E_i,j. If w=sum_i c_i e_i is a nonzero vector in W, choose i with c_i nonzero. Then E_ji w=c_i e_j for every j, so every basis vector belongs to W and W is the whole module. Its dimension lambda+1 is positive. This proves the result, including lambda=0, without requiring p>2 or distinct reduced h-weights.\\\",\\\"source_obligations\\\":\\\"No literature theorem is imported. The divided-power formulas follow by iteration from the supplied sl2 relations and highest-weight equations. Matrix-unit identities and R-module arguments are derived in the proof. The characteristic-zero basis and dimension, lattice properties, and action setup are supplied by the frozen context and hypotheses.\\\",\\\"edge_cases\\\":\\\"lambda=0 gives a one-dimensional module with identity matrix unit. For p=2, lambda is 0 or 1; no division by 2 occurs. The proof treats every admissible lattice and every field K of characteristic p by extension from F_p.\\\"}\"}","status":"completed"}}

